      "content": "Even if your arms and legs feel fine, facial drooping requires prompt medical evaluation to rule out serious issues. Bells palsy is a nerve issue, but a stroke can sometimes present with isolated facial symptoms initially. Since you are experiencing any change in facial function, the safest and most responsible action is to have a doctor assess you immediately. Do not wait to see if it gets better on its own.",
      "source": "target",
